		<author><name><![CDATA[VK3KYY]]></name></author>
		<updated>2023-03-15T21:57:06</updated>

		<published>2023-03-15T21:57:06</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2760&amp;p=22621#p22621</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2760&amp;p=22621#p22621"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Firmware installation instructions]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2760&amp;p=22621#p22621"><![CDATA[
Follow the TYT MD UV380 / Retevis RT-3S instructions<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=19&amp;t=2380" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=19&amp;t=2380</a><br><br>Except select DM-1701/ RT-84 as the radio and use the DM-1701 firmware.<br>Note. At the moment becuase the DM-1701 and RT-84 share the same internal hardware the same firmware file is used on both DM-1701 and RT-84<br><br>However the plastic case of the DM-1701 and RT-84 have slightly different aperatures for the LCD display, so that on the DM-1701 the top 4 pixels of the display are obscured.  So in the longer term there may need to be different firmware versions so that the DM-1701 uses less of the screen height, and will have one less menu item displayed.<br><br>Official 'donor' firmware is the same as the UV380<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Mar 15, 2023 9:57 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
